From 9e74ba40324471582108e4b842731acf4c5c1f44 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: FreeholdOS Build <build@freeholdos.local>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 20:48:35 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 16/16] compartments: give back the location permissions that
 the service took

revokeLocation took the location permissions of an app whose location is Blocked or whose
persona cannot be made, and nothing gave them back: an app set from Blocked to Real data stayed
without the permission that the user had granted (CMP-015, lynx 2026103101). A ledger
(RevokedLedger, /data/system/compartments/revoked, 0600) now notes each permission that the app
held when it was taken, and restoreLocation grants it again once the package is no longer denied.
Only a granted permission is noted, so nothing is granted that the user did not hold; the file can
name only the four location permissions; a missing or damaged file leaves the permissions revoked.
